  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $213M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department awarded 245 contracts so far, with an average award size of $868K. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. The Department’s FY2027 to date total is small compared with prior fiscal years: FY22 totaled $9.3B, FY23 totaled $10.3B, FY24 totaled $9.3B, FY25 totaled $8.6B, and FY26 totaled $7B. The FY2027 to date picture shows concentration in a few categories and vendors. Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining is the largest category at $91.7M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is the largest vendor at $91.7M. Software, data processing, and other computer-related services appear among the top categories but at much smaller totals than the metal and paper sectors. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 obligations much lower than prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $213M in FY2027 to date, versus multi-billion dollar totals in FY22 through FY26. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. The FY2027 to date total is partial and represents fiscal year to date obligations, which explains part of the year-over-year gap."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Treasury spending concentrated in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining is the largest category at $91.7M. STONEX FINANCIAL LTD is the largest vendor at $91.7M, followed by CRANE & CO., INC. at $20.4M and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $17.9M. Other notable categories include Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $32.6M and Other Computer Related Services at $24.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Treasury spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury obligated $213M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department made 245 awards, with an average award size of $868K. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year, and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Treasury buy?",
      "a": "Treasury buys a mix of industrial, manufacturing, and IT-related goods and services. The largest category in FY2027 to date is Nonferrous Metal (except Aluminum) Smelting and Refining at $91.7M, followed by Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $32.6M, and Other Computer Related Services at $24.1M. Paper Mills, Software Publishers, and computing infrastructure services also appear among the top categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Treasury's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Treasury's largest contractors in FY2027 to date are STONEX FINANCIAL LTD at $91.7M, CRANE & CO., INC. at $20.4M, and WIELAND ROLLED PRODUCTS NORTH AMERICA, LLC at $17.9M. Other top vendors include PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. at $14.7M and FCN, INC. at $8.9M."
